# 14.0

* [brainscales2-demos]
  * add `jaxsnn` introductory demo
  * enable downloading nightly calibration
  * adapt demos to PyNN `Compartment` renaming, pre-access mapping requirement, refractory period naming consistency, and Lui task ordering
* [calix]
  * add `spiking3` nightly calibration and fix weekly calibration (for jaxsnn intro demo)
  * add CADC characterization via external DAC, CADC/MADC parameter translation, and restructured MADC characterization
  * add `Polynomial`, `Polynomial1D`, `InterpolatingCollection`, `Collection2D`, `Transformation`, `Domain`, `Linear`, and `CapacitanceInFarad` types
  * fix `tau_mem` calibration (re-enable synaptic input beforehand), per-neuron `high_resistance` in `tau_syn` calibration, `tau_icc` serialization in calibration targets, and scalar `synapse_dac_bias` handling
* [grenade]
  * multi-chip support: population partitioning and placement across multiple chips (`PopulationTopologyRewrite`), round-robin external source distribution, multi-chip routing loops, and multi-chip results in `RoutingResult`
  * add `InterChipRouter`, `InputRoutingTable`, and `OutputRoutingTable` vertices with chip config visitors and multi-chip barriers before realtime sections
  * multi-compartment (MC) neurons: topology rewrite, bridge insertion, DFS branch placement, morphology builder tree enforcement, Python bindings for `Leak`/`Fire` mechanisms and compartment queries, and physical capacitance units per compartment in `CalibratedNeuron`
  * move scheduling and time-related plasticity functions to internal memory, size scheduler queue to timer count, and fix time definition ordering
  * fix PAD, MADC, and CADC recorder channel selection, honor `CalibratedNeuron` readout sources, add `TopologyLazyValidityChecker`, and fix GCC 13 / C++20 builds
* [hxtorch]
  * mock mode: add infrastructure for event drops, weight discretization, bounds, random noise, and fixed-pattern noise (with hardware-unaware backward pass)
  * add synaptic input readout support, require per-atomic-neuron readout sources, adapt to physical capacitance units in `grenade`, and require float neuron parameters with `ConversionConfig` in NIR conversion
  * make handles pickleable, use persistent output handles, refactor `AELIF` handle assembly, and fix `networkx` memory issues
* [jaxsnn]
  * introduce topology builder API for arbitrary architectures and expose calibration in topology
  * add `to_nir` conversion utility, fix `from_nir` conversion, and add the `SHD` dataset
  * replace matrix exponential with closed-form/eigen flows, replace `cond`/`switch` constructs, and clean up TTFS solver (supporting simultaneous spikes and nonzero leak)
  * support newer JAX versions (`>= 0.12`), multi-Python-version pip builds, and dynamic versioning
* [lib-rcf] fix data race during worker reinitialization by operating on copied data
* [pynn-brainscales]
  * multi-compartment (MC) API: add morphology builder, common MC neuron base class, MC projections, CADC/MADC multi-compartment recording, readout source selection, and an MC example
  * manage plasticity readout settings, enforce initial config before parameter access without overwriting defaults, adapt to physical capacitance units in `grenade`, and fix analog readout source selection
  * remove deprecated `pynn.preprocess()` usage from tests/examples and document hardware connection requirement for `pynn.run`

# 13.0

* [grenade] New experiment description and mapping in grenade 💣
  * network interface is removed and superseeded by Topology-based interface
  * signal_flow.{Graph,Vertex} interface is removed and superseeded by Topology-based interface
  * enables interoperability of the model and hardware graph
  * GreedyMapper:
    * partitioning and placement are performed algorithmically
    * JITCalibration: calibration is performed via calix after partitioning and placement
  * signal_flow.pack_spikes is removed
  * Python-based front end adapter is added
  * Execution{Health,Time}Info are (partially) replaced by ExecutionInstanceGlobal and ExecutorGlobal
  * execution.run can execute hardware/signal_flow-level topologies, mapping from more abstract representations is happening in user code (or the front end adapter) now
* [pynn-brainscales] adapting to grenade
  * preprocess() always requires executor access now. Therefore, we enable using the ZeroMock connection for software tests
  * get_execution_{time,health}_info() is replaced by get_execution_instance_data() -> grenade.common.OutputData.ExecutionInstances
  * Projection.placed_connections return type changes
  * SpikeIOSourcePopulation support is temporarily disabled
* [hxtorch] adapting to grenade
  * PyTorch independent code is moved into core namespace, including:
    * Experiment base class
    * base population and projection
    * Morphology
    * Observables
    * Parameters
    * Calibration helper functions
  * Adds mixin for trainable parameter types
  * Adds an option to enable constant current onto neurons
  * Spilts spiking.types into spiking.types.{population, projection}
  * Removes obsolete NeuronPlacement
  * Removes ExecutionInstance
  * Replaced native calix calibration with cocolist to be more resilient to calix changes
  * Enables projection to either be signed or unsigned
  * Adds plasticity class
  * Drop support for perceptron.InferenceTracer, since not used anymore
* [calix]
  * move CalibrationTargets to C++
    * allows interfacing in e.g. grenade
    * more typesafety
    * dropped non-array supplication of targets
    * change time unit in targets from us to s
    * the target serialization changes, so the calibration
  * cache gets invalidated, since the hash changes. (also applies to nightly deployed calibration)
* [jaxsnn]
  * temporarily drops hardware support

# 12.0

* [brainscales2-demos] adapting to API changes and minor updates (exp. LIF demo and fI-curve, Lui, BSS2 docs, comp. neurosci. demo)
* [calix] optimizations for QuiggeldyConnection; int. cap. char.; inter-comp. conductance, madc char., parallelization of fits
* [fisch] adapt to hxcomm::MultiConnection
* [haldls] multi-chip tests; integration of hxcomm::MultiConnection
* [hxtorch] add ExpSumOverTime decoder; add lead_conductance neuron parameter; minor fixes
* [pynn-brainscales] support for SpikeIO RX (OffChipSource)

